"""Terminal UI that assembles and starts an `ansible-navigator run` of an LFOps playbook.

Steps: playbook > tags > inventories > limit > confirm. Playbooks, tags, inventories and
hosts are read from the LFOps checkout and the inventories, the entries used last are
listed first. Further arguments are passed on to ansible-navigator, for example
`lfops --check --diff`.

With `eval "$(command lfops --shell-init bash)"` in `~/.bashrc` (or `zsh` in
`~/.zshrc`), the command lands on the shell prompt and in the history instead of running
right away.

Installation, environment variables, keys and the shell integration: see
tools/README.md.
"""

